they will make you do it again.

204
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:06,960
She'll say, "Ruonan, do that again."

205
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:08,400
"We can't air it like this."

206
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:10,760
(OMG, you scared me!)
Really?

207
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:12,160
(Just kidding)
I'm kidding.

208
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:14,840
(Cute little rabbit)
I should look scared to look at people.

209
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:16,520
Right. You have to act very stiff.

210
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:24,200
(So adorable)
So cute!

211
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:26,680
Why are you so cute?

212
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:28,160
Too cute.

213
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:30,460
(Ke Uh-Oh has arrived)

214
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:32,200
This is Keyu. Have you met before?

215
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:32,600
I just met him.

216
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:33,120
Just now.

217
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:33,840
(Introducing Nan)
The one we just filmed with.

218
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:34,680
First time meeting?

219
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:35,120
Yeah.

220
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:37,120
It really is our first time.

221
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:39,240
It's my first time meeting both of you.

222
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:40,160
Yeah.

223
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:41,040
How does it feel?

224
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:42,240
Meeting for the first time.

225
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:44,080
(Happy)
Yeah, it's nice.

226
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:45,800
Your ears are perking up.

227
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,160
(Happy puppy)
Yeah.

228
00:06:50,140 --> 00:06:51,180
(Found a "new continent")

229
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,040
Don't.

230
00:06:54,020 --> 00:06:54,880
(Found something incredible)

231
00:06:54,880 --> 00:06:56,920
(Detective Fox is on duty)
Why are you so naughty?

232
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:58,840
(Staying in character)
What? We're staying in character.

233
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:00,080
Little corgi.

234
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,680
Who's a little corgi?

235
00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:03,980
(Behaving now)

236
00:07:04,020 --> 00:07:06,300
(Someone's always
having fun in the dark)

237
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:08,240
I'm here.

238
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:10,280
Where are you guys?

239
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:11,080
(Night vision mode. This fictional story
contains horror elements)

240
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:11,880
I can't understand

241
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:14,280
(Master of mishearing)
a single word he's saying.

242
00:07:14,280 --> 00:07:16,640
(Hope someone helps)
Anyone? I can't hear a word.

243
00:07:18,420 --> 00:07:19,420
(Peeks out)

244
00:07:19,420 --> 00:07:21,450
(Night vision mode. This fictional story
contains horror elements)

245
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:22,700
(Looks around)

246
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:28,060
(Tries the door)

247
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:34,050
(Night vision mode. This fictional story
contains horror elements)

248
00:07:34,060 --> 00:07:35,780
(Out of ideas)

249
00:07:37,460 --> 00:07:39,150
(Shaking)
Oh my god.

250
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:40,560
Oh my god.

251
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:41,740
(Poor kid's freaking out)

252
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:45,700
(Needs a deep breath)

253
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:51,180
(Feels safer leaning here)

254
00:07:52,780 --> 00:07:54,740
(Defense mode on)

255
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:58,980
(Courage restoring)

256
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:06,080
Pray, pray.

257
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:09,120
(Sincere prayer)
It's okay.

258
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:11,260
(Looks calm)

259
00:08:11,260 --> 00:08:14,100
(Manually mutes headset. Missed two)

260
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:16,400
(Ning mumbling)
I can't hear. I can't see.

261
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,680
Don't scare me.

262
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:22,100
(Hides by squatting)

263
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:29,220
(Cool as ever)

264
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:37,120
I knew it.

265
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:38,220
(Wolf King's prediction)

266
00:08:41,340 --> 00:08:43,540
(This is fun)

267
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:47,660
(Sneaks a peek)

268
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:50,020
(That was close)

269
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:53,200
(Worried about the NPC)
That must've hurt.

270
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:53,860
Are you okay?

271
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,520
(An actual angel)

272
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:57,360
(Please spare me)
It should be over now, right?

273
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:59,080
Can I come out now?

274
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:04,360
(Door's locked)
I can't get out. It's locked.

275
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:07,400
The door's locked.

276
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:09,880
The door's locked, guys.

277
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:11,440
Did you all get out?

278
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,280
No.

279
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:15,400
(Newbie needs help)
How do I get out?

280
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:17,640
(Something feels really off)
Why isn't anyone talking?

281
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:19,880
(Finally realizes)
Is He Struggle there?

282
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:21,880
(No response)

283
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:22,960
He Struggle.

284
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,280
He Struggle?

285
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:26,600
Capybara!

286
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:27,860
(Still calling teammate)

287
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,560
He's gone.

288
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:30,440
We're done.

289
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,680
(He got a solo mission)
A solo mission.

290
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:36,560
He Struggle, are you there?

291
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:37,680
(Scared but acting calm)
He Struggle!

292
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:38,800
He Struggle?

293
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:40,080
Capybara!

294
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,760
A solo mission.

295
00:09:42,020 --> 00:09:44,020
(Stays quiet)

296
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:44,840
Ke?

297
00:09:45,380 --> 00:09:45,860
(Another misheard member +1)

298
00:09:45,860 --> 00:09:46,400
Ke?

299
00:09:47,220 --> 00:09:47,900
(Always gets a reply)

300
00:09:48,050 --> 00:09:48,720
Ke!

301
00:09:49,150 --> 00:09:49,740
Ke?

302
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:52,040
Ke disappeared too.

303
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:54,360
(What's wrong with him today?)
He's not here.

304
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:55,840
Ke?

305
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,560
(Finally hears something)
What?

306
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:06,060
(Laughter is my shield)

307
00:10:08,380 --> 00:10:11,020
(This is interesting)

308
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:13,140
(Calm)

309
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:16,640
Finally out.

310
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:17,640
We can leave now.

311
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:18,760
Are you okay, Jin?

312
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:19,660
(Worried about her)

313
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,160
You okay?

314
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:25,020
(Checks on her first)

315
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:25,880
He.

316
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,080
Where's He?

317
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:30,220
(I'm here)

318
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:32,680
What were you pretending for?

319
00:10:32,680 --> 00:10:35,360
I thought you were gone.

320
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:37,280
Why weren't you two talking?

321
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:40,160
(Scared)
You scared me. I thought it was a solo mission.

322
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:43,380
(Just loves messing around)

323
00:10:43,420 --> 00:10:45,700
(Longdong Army spirit lives on)

324
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:47,840
I think the three of us

325
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:50,280
already showed it.

326
00:10:50,280 --> 00:10:51,080
So next...

327
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:51,820
(You two)

328
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:53,280
Should we do it separately?

329
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:54,120
I overestimated myself

330
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,000
on this one.

331
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,600
I think you two can handle it too.

332
00:10:58,040 --> 00:10:59,160
We're already here. Might as well try.

333
00:10:59,160 --> 00:10:59,980
(Worth the trip)

334
00:10:59,980 --> 00:11:01,440
(Makes sense)

335
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:03,240
So who's coming with us?

336
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:05,040
He Struggle's coming with you.

337
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:06,400
Yeah, He Struggle.

338
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:08,120
He Struggle was just...

339
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:09,920
Where's Longdong Army?

340
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:12,080
Yeah. Where's Longdong Army?

341
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:13,440
Longdong Army's here!

342
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,400
(Longdong Army spirit)
Longdong Army's here. Don't be scared.

343
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:16,880
(Who can resist Longdong Army?)
Come on!

344
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:18,080
Come on.

345
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:19,680
Longdong Army.

346
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:20,720
Longdong Army!

347
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:22,280
(Let's go!)
Longdong Army!

348
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:23,560
(Fight!)
Longdong Army!

349
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:25,200
What's Longdong Army?

350
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,280
It's our team spirit.

351
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:29,480
Battle mode activated.

352
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:33,120
Longdong Army!

353
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:34,400
Longdong Army.

354
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:35,520
Longdong Army!

355
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:36,660
(Sound of victory)
Hmph.

356
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:38,540
(Battle begins)

357
00:11:39,380 --> 00:11:40,060
Ah!

358
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:40,800
No!

359
00:11:40,860 --> 00:11:42,420
Ah!

360
00:11:44,060 --> 00:11:45,300
Hahaha!

361
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:48,280
I'm drooling.

362
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:50,340
Ah!

363
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:51,360
Wait!

364
00:11:51,660 --> 00:11:52,620
Ah!

365
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:54,360
(Bump)
Wait!

366
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:02,660
(Leaving the prep area)

367
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:03,600
Battle failed.

368
00:12:04,940 --> 00:12:07,700
(Where's the Qide Longdong Potion?)

369
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:08,920
If I put my pants on,

370
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:10,200
he's definitely not winning today.

371
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:11,040
Why?

372
00:12:11,040 --> 00:12:12,200
You're trying to kick someone's face.

373
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:13,800
(Wild imagination)
You can kick their face with pants on?

374
00:12:15,060 --> 00:12:15,840
Longdong Army!

375
00:12:16,170 --> 00:12:17,040
Longdong Army.

376
00:12:17,260 --> 00:12:18,200
Longdong Army!

377
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:19,180
What does Longdong Army mean?

378
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:20,690
You wouldn't understand.

379
00:12:21,530 --> 00:12:22,350
You just wouldn't.

380
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:23,800
Longdong Army!

381
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:25,600
Longdong Army.

382
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:27,200
(Instantly fired up)
Longdong Army!

383
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:28,320
Longdong Army!

384
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:30,580
(Everything is Longdong Army)
Longdong Army!

385
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:33,480
System question.

386
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,840
Why do the players
keep shouting "Longdong Army"?

387
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:38,000
We're not telling you.

388
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,360
It's our secret.

389
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:40,880
(A little secret among the players)
We can't tell you.

390
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,480
Actually, Longdong Army

391
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:45,040
expresses our feelings

392
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:46,680
for the characters

393
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:47,920
we played last episode.

394
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:49,680
That's right. It's a tribute.

395
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:51,240
To honor their selflessness.

396
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:52,560
Every time I say "Longdong Army",

397
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:54,120
it fills me with positive energy.

398
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:56,100
(The spirit lives on)

399
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:57,700
(I see)

400
00:12:57,740 --> 00:13:00,020
(The magic revealed. Always looking out)

401
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:01,680
Everyone, have a seat.

402
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:04,200
The ritual's about to begin.

403
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:07,040
Time to punish her.

404
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:07,920
How?

405
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:08,720
Cut off half of it.

406
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:10,280
(Ning figured it out)
It's probably magic.

407
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:13,080
The upper body is here.

408
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,000
The lower body is down here.

409
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,240
See that?

410
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:17,400
Magic.

411
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:23,820
(Magic prop.
Dramatic use only. Do not imitate)

412
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:24,580
(I wasn't mentally prepared enough.)

413
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:25,900
(Surprised JPG)

414
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:30,560
Why doesn't the knife come out
from the back?

415
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,680
(Mumbling)
Does it retract and extend?

416
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:33,800
It retracts and extends.

417
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:34,720
(It's "retractable")
It retracts and extends.

418
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:36,840
The soft blade goes through
from the back.

419
00:13:38,380 --> 00:13:42,580
(Intense discussion)

420
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:43,400
And then?

421
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:44,560
Excuse me.

422
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:47,960
Our supporting actress

423
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:48,760
(Holding the pose too long)
can't hold on much longer.

424
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:49,800
Let's let her leave the stage.

425
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:50,480
Okay, sure.

426
00:13:50,480 --> 00:13:50,920
Quick.

427
00:13:50,920 --> 00:13:52,080
Please cooperate.

428
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:53,000
(Acting quickly)
Need any help?

429
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:53,840
Are you okay?

430
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:54,800
Just move aside.

431
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:56,480
The director is coming in.

432
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:57,720
You should've said that earlier.

433
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:58,080
Yeah, earlier.

434
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:01,720
Help quickly.

435
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:02,840
(Concerned)
Support her.

436
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:06,040
That was tough.

437
00:14:06,040 --> 00:14:07,400
That was really tough.

438
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:08,480
Is she okay?

439
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:12,680
Take it slow.

440
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:14,180
(Unable to stand steadily)

441
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:16,120
Come on.

442
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:17,160
(Quickly stepping in to help)
It's been too long.

443
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:19,400
Come.

444
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:21,400
(Let her rest first)
Okay.

445
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:22,280
Are you okay?

446
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:24,240
Why don't you take your hands out first?

447
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:25,160
Yeah, rest for a bit.

448
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:28,120
(Helping untie the ropes)
Can you come down?

449
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:28,680
This one... okay.

450
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:31,640
You can't come down yet.

451
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:32,880
Just stand straight. It's okay.

452
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:33,380
(Offering a solution)

453
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:36,600
You can untie his rope.

454
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:37,800
Let him fall onto the ground.

455
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:38,680
Yeah, just lie down.

456
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:39,360
Okay.

457
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:40,760
Lie down.

458
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:41,400
Lie down first.

459
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:41,960
Sit in the corner.

460
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:42,840
Make yourself comfortable.

461
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:43,560
Sit down.

462
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:44,680
Lean against the pillar.

463
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:45,560
There's a pillar there.

464
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:46,640
(Warm reminder)
Just lean on it.

465
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:47,520
Forget about that.

466
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:48,440
Thanks for your hard work.

467
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:49,720
(Concerned)
Thanks.

468
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:51,280
I saw you move just now.

469
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:52,960
I was secretly spotted.

470
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:53,400
Thanks.

471
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:53,920
Thank you.

472
00:14:53,920 --> 00:14:54,960
Thanks.

473
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:55,920
Go stretch when you get back.

474
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:57,760
(Warm reminder)
Yeah, whoever's autograph you want,

475
00:14:57,760 --> 00:14:59,560
the staff will get it for you later.

476
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:01,200
(I'll handle it for you)
Thanks.

477
00:15:02,260 --> 00:15:04,540
(It's about me and you)

478
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:06,000
I really want to watch the movie.

479
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,040
Do you want to watch it?

480
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:07,760
I'm a little nervous.

481
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:08,280
(Airing now: "Missing You")
I'm a little scared.

482
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:09,080
I really want to watch it.

483
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:10,120
When you showed me the film,

484
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:10,920
if it made me feel

485
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:11,760
that it was really good,

486
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:12,680
I'd be so excited.

487
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:13,720
Don't say that. I'm a little nervous.

488
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:14,600
You know, the day it was announced,

489
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:16,040
I really cried.

490
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:17,240
In my room.

491
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:18,400
Because you were excited?

492
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:19,960
No, because I was scared.

493
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,720
I'm here. What are you afraid of?

494
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:23,080
(Don't worry, leave it to me)
I'm afraid I'll hold you back.

495
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:24,560
(Worried about affecting Nan)
You're going to cry again, aren't you?

496
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:26,800
You always act so humble with me.

497
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:29,000
The two of us.
If you make it, I make it.

498
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,160
If I make it, you make it.

499
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:31,280
How wonderful you are,

500
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:32,400
the audience will see it

501
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:33,640
through my eyes.

502
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:35,320
The two of us are like,
you succeed, I succeed.

503
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:37,680
(We stand together)
If you fall, I fall. Got it?

504
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:38,560
Well said.

505
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:39,520
That's the truth.

506
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:40,280
I want to cry again.

507
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:41,320
Then cry now.

508
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:42,280
I really want to cry.

509
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,560
Cry for me right now.

510
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:44,920
I want to see
how expensive your makeup is.

511
00:15:45,260 --> 00:15:46,540
(Teary-eyed)

512
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:48,560
Okay.

513
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:49,760
(We can be ordinary)
You really cried.

514
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:50,960
(We don't have to be perfect)
So cute.

515
00:15:50,960 --> 00:15:52,000
(Because we should enjoy our lives)
Really.

516
00:15:52,020 --> 00:15:54,300
(Will we ever find this ultimate clue?)

517
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:56,640
So why did his severed limb

518
00:15:56,640 --> 00:15:59,640
have a print on it?

519
00:15:59,640 --> 00:16:00,720
It was meant to point
to the mysterious zone.

520
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:01,520
Yes.

521
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:03,400
It was only to lead us
to the mysterious zone.

522
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:05,960
Then why is the mysterious zone
a dog print?

523
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:06,480
A puppy.

524
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:08,920
(A silent performance)
A cat has the same kind of paw print.

525
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:11,640
(Who is framing who?)
You really want me to be the killer.

526
00:16:11,640 --> 00:16:14,480
(A wounded heart)
You really hurt me today.

527
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:15,760
No, listen.

528
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:17,880
The part where we looked for the fish.

529
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:20,920
I was really hurt
during that part today.

530
00:16:20,920 --> 00:16:21,920
I saw Zhou Keyu's back

531
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:23,440
looking so anxious.

532
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:24,440
I walked closer and heard him.

533
00:16:24,440 --> 00:16:25,960
He was asking if fish can see at night.

534
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:26,720
Can fish see at night?

535
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:28,640
(Jin heard everything)
Did you find any fish information?

536
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:29,720
Killer.

537
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:32,360
(Neither is better)
What gives you the right to question me?

538
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:33,880
(You're panicking)
Your reaction is off.

539
00:16:34,880 --> 00:16:35,640
Really?

540
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:37,160
Yes.

541
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:39,120
(My ears)
Killer.

542
00:16:39,120 --> 00:16:40,840
What is extreme regeneration?

543
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:43,440
It is the regeneration of nerve
and muscle cells.

544
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:46,400
For example, canines and reindeer.

545
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:48,000
(Seriously asking)
Are there fish species too?

546
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:51,200
Fish species? What does fish have?

547
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:52,120
She can't see.

548
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:53,520
(I heard everything)
I heard that.

549
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:55,760
Yes, it can actually clear you.

550
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:57,880
No means you're in.

551
00:16:57,900 --> 00:16:58,840
(Then you're in danger)

552
00:16:58,840 --> 00:17:00,480
Let me test you.

553
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:01,560
(Q&A time)
Since you're a beluga whale,

554
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:04,000
whales live deep in the ocean,
where it's so dark.

555
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,280
Can they see there?

556
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,760
Let me explain.

557
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:08,960
No, it's because in the ocean...

558
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:10,400
It's okay.
I just wanted to see if she knew.

559
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:12,160
If I were in the water,

560
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:14,400
then it couldn't possibly be me.

561
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:14,760
Why?

562
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:15,240
She doesn't know.

563
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:16,440
Because I'm in the water.

564
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:18,000
No. It's radar.

565
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,600
(That's not related)
Because whales don't rely on their eyes.

566
00:17:19,600 --> 00:17:21,800
(Ke's mini lesson)
They use sonar positioning.

567
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:24,080
You guys showed off again.

568
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:25,200
Do you know how

569
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:26,040
this person found out?

570
00:17:26,060 --> 00:17:27,400
(First-row gossip scene)

571
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:28,840
I went to the bathroom
with Ning earlier.

572
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:30,640
(The power of knowledge)
Ning kept looking things up.

573
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:32,720
He looked up
what family whales belong to.

574
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:34,200
The answer was the whale species.

575
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:35,200
(Misheard little rabbit)
What are whale species?

576
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,760
Whale species means whales.

577
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:38,360
Capybaras are rodents.

578
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:40,200
Capybaras are aquatic rodents.

579
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,600
(Capybara)
That are rodents.

580
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:42,240
(Part of the capybara family)
Yes.

581
00:17:42,240 --> 00:17:43,240
(The world's largest rodent)

582
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:45,720
It feels like things
are going smoothly today.

583
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:47,880
Didn't you two get called away halfway?

584
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:48,560
Then they told you

585
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:50,000
who the killer was.

586
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:54,840
(A fake move)
My director told me who the killer is.

587
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,560
(Do you think I believe you?)
No way.

588
00:17:57,560 --> 00:18:00,000
They called you out
just to tell you that?

589
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,200
She said later we should
avoid mentioning that person.

590
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:04,280
(Stay in character)
Because this round is too easy.

591
00:18:04,280 --> 00:18:05,540
(Joining the group)
Too easy.

592
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:06,940
(No way I believe that)

593
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:08,660
(Watching you perform quietly)

594
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:11,060
(Actually believed it)

595
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:13,000
Right?

596
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,320
(Completely convinced)
I remember you told me.

597
00:18:14,320 --> 00:18:17,240
(Little fox takes over)
Yes, they told us who the killer was.

598
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:19,120
(Can't hold it in)

599
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:21,200
I'm someone who trusts people easily.

600
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,680
No, nobody would play like that.

601
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:24,120
How do we even play this?

602
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:25,660
(Confirmed innocent little rabbit)

603
00:18:25,660 --> 00:18:26,800
(Ning arrives)

604
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:28,720
Ning, I'm really hurt.

605
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:29,720
Why?

606
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:32,840
I heard you've been
investigating whales.

607
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:34,120
(The kind that can't be comforted)
I'm really hurt.

608
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:35,680
I can't let you win two rounds in a row.

609
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,040
That would make us look bad.

610
00:18:37,040 --> 00:18:38,200
Jin, you won yesterday?

611
00:18:39,900 --> 00:18:41,500
(That's my amazing girl)

612
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:44,720
(Dramatic use only. Do not imitate)
Let's see if any of these are key clues.

613
00:18:44,720 --> 00:18:46,280
(Searching the electrical box again)
What's this?

614
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:46,920
This is fur.

615
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:47,680
Fur?

616
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:49,880
Is this capybara fur?

617
00:18:49,880 --> 00:18:50,600
(Suspected to be He Struggle's fur)

618
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:51,560
Because the capybara...

619
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:53,680
Because the capybara shed its fur.

620
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:55,880
You blew away the key evidence.

621
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:56,800
It shed fur.

622
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:58,000
What's wrong?

623
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,360
We found key evidence belonging to you.

624
00:19:03,620 --> 00:19:04,780
(Bunbun is happy)

625
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:06,400
Remember what you just said.

626
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:08,080
Record it and say it again.

627
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:08,760
What did you just say?

628
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:10,120
I said we found

629
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:11,760
He Struggle's key evidence.

630
00:19:11,760 --> 00:19:13,040
So who gets the credit for finding it?

631
00:19:13,100 --> 00:19:13,840
(Dramatic use only. Do not imitate)

632
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:15,160
No, let's think about this again.

633
00:19:15,160 --> 00:19:15,720
(Lost in thought)
Look at this fur again.

634
00:19:15,720 --> 00:19:16,240
Take another look.

635
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:16,680
Is this really fur?

636
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:17,640
If we had found that yesterday...

637
00:19:17,640 --> 00:19:18,520
Did you see it?

638
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:19,680
This fur definitely isn't it.

639
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:20,240
(Big misunderstanding)
This fur definitely isn't it.

640
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:22,680
His fur is brown.

641
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:24,160
Look.

642
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:25,920
(Please let the heavens judge me)
Now I see who believes me.

643
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:29,000
Wait, let me check the capybara.

644
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:30,520
His fur is brown.

645
00:19:30,520 --> 00:19:32,160
Her diary had that fur.

646
00:19:32,160 --> 00:19:34,160
It was the long brown fur.

647
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:35,600
Long fur.

648
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:36,400
I'll remember the three of you

649
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:38,720
(Hurtful words)
and how you acted at this moment.

650
00:19:39,620 --> 00:19:42,820
(Nan is laughing like crazy)

651
00:19:42,840 --> 00:19:44,080
Okay.

652
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:47,280
What?

653
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:50,200
Nothing. There's a frog here.

654
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:51,320
(Zoomed in 300%)
It scared me.

655
00:19:51,320 --> 00:19:52,120
It's looking at me.

656
00:19:52,120 --> 00:19:53,160
Are you afraid of frogs?

657
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:54,000
I'm not.

658
00:19:56,940 --> 00:19:57,660
Hehe.

659
00:19:57,980 --> 00:19:59,020
Ribbit, ribbit.

660
00:19:59,480 --> 00:20:00,360
Let's go.

661
00:20:00,360 --> 00:20:01,840
Let's go. Don't disturb it.

662
00:20:01,840 --> 00:20:02,160
Let's go.

663
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:03,160
(So polite)
Carry it away for it.

664
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:03,800
You carry it.

665
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:04,600
It'll leave.

666
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:06,200
It can find its own home.

667
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:06,920
Don't stand there.

668
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:07,480
It won't dare come over.

669
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:09,360
The frog is looking for its mom.
Let's go.

670
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:10,520
Which way?

671
00:20:10,520 --> 00:20:11,960
We need to go up.

672
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:12,320
This way.

673
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:13,160
(Wrong direction)
The one just now.

674
00:20:13,160 --> 00:20:14,200
Okay.

675
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:14,720
Sorry.

676
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:16,480
We'll walk over there.

677
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:17,080
Don't disturb it.

678
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:18,400
Let's not disturb it.

679
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:19,600
It's going to find its mom.

680
00:20:19,600 --> 00:20:21,400
The tadpole is looking for its mom.

681
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:23,280
Why haven't those two come over yet?

682
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:24,320
(Two detectives disconnected)
Looking for key evidence.

683
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:25,640
Where did they go?

684
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:27,800
(Searching for clues)
Could there be a key clue here?

685
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:29,920
I think when he hid the body,

686
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:31,240
