687
00:20:31,240 --> 00:20:33,480
What if we really just missed it?

688
00:20:33,480 --> 00:20:33,960
Right.

689
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:35,240
We're both idiots.

690
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:36,800
(Can't let this happen)
Keep searching.

691
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:38,080
Is there anything inside this lid?

692
00:20:38,080 --> 00:20:39,160
(Very serious)
Shine a light on it.

693
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:39,800
They went ahead.

694
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:41,160
It's okay, we'll catch up.

695
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:42,120
Close this.

696
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:42,760
No.

697
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:44,800
We have to find the key clue.

698
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:45,600
But wait.

699
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:46,640
What are these bottles for?

700
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:47,400
I want to know.

701
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:48,760
(Leaving no suspicious detail behind)
Yeah, why are there so many bottles?

702
00:20:48,760 --> 00:20:51,160
That corrosive agent
needs to dissolve in water.

703
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:53,920
Only after dissolving in water
can it corrode him.

704
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:56,640
One small bottle of it
wouldn't be enough.

705
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:57,720
No.

706
00:20:57,720 --> 00:21:00,240
(Too many bottles)
Then he prepared way too many bottles.

707
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:03,520
Yeah, so many bottles of water.

708
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:04,640
Look here.

709
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:06,360
Take a look here.

710
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:09,280
(So persistent)
What's this?

711
00:21:09,280 --> 00:21:10,720
This is fur.

712
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:11,600
There really is fur.

713
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:14,160
Don't do this.

714
00:21:14,160 --> 00:21:15,760
We're already seeing fur everywhere.

715
00:21:15,760 --> 00:21:16,640
(Everything looks like fur)
Everything looks like fur.

716
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:18,480
No, it really is fur.

717
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:19,680
This really is fur.

718
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:22,040
Is it my fur?

719
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:24,160
(No shedding problems)
I don't shed.

720
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:24,680
Let me tell you.

721
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:26,560
(Wolf King breaks the tank)
The best way is we poured out the water.

722
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:28,120
Wait, what's this?

723
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:30,240
We're scaring ourselves.

724
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:32,200
No, I think the key clue is right near

725
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:33,600
where he committed the crime.

726
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:34,640
Definitely. Because...

727
00:21:34,640 --> 00:21:35,320
Do you remember?

728
00:21:35,320 --> 00:21:38,080
Every time we found a clue,

729
00:21:38,080 --> 00:21:40,720
it was always nearby.

730
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:42,520
Think about the last one.

731
00:21:42,520 --> 00:21:43,760
(Case 7: Reborn as a Living Treasure)
The thread. And the one before?

732
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:46,200
(Case 5: Will we find the Qide Sword?)
It was the killer's sword.

733
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,040
The killer's sword.

734
00:21:47,040 --> 00:21:48,320
It was in the box.

735
00:21:48,940 --> 00:21:51,220
(He remember everything clearly)

736
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:53,360
Then I was the seal.

737
00:21:53,360 --> 00:21:53,960
The seal.

738
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:54,640
It shattered.

739
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:55,680
(Case 6: Everyone Has a Secret Identity)
We all touched this thing.

740
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:58,200
Yeah, I was the one playing with it.

741
00:21:58,200 --> 00:21:59,480
And at the very beginning.

742
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:00,400
(Case 2: Oh No, Not the Puppet)
The pen. Using the pen to draw.

743
00:22:00,400 --> 00:22:01,360
Using the pen to draw.

744
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:02,120
(Case 4: Undercover in a Scam Factory)
On the phone.

745
00:22:02,120 --> 00:22:02,720
On the phone.

746
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:03,760
(Case 3: The Price of 0.99)
Then in the trash can.

747
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:04,560
(Case 1: My Family Is a Total Mess)
The trash can.

748
00:22:05,500 --> 00:22:06,220
Oh my god.

749
00:22:06,220 --> 00:22:07,160
Oh my.

750
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:07,980
(I missed too many clues)

751
00:22:08,180 --> 00:22:08,960
(Waiting for the result)

752
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:09,640
I feel like

753
00:22:09,640 --> 00:22:11,960
today's key evidence was so close to me.

754
00:22:11,960 --> 00:22:15,120
Yeah, I feel it was
in those bottles and tanks.

755
00:22:15,120 --> 00:22:16,760
Maybe it was right on them.

756
00:22:16,760 --> 00:22:19,120
You really... You're obsessed with this.

757
00:22:19,120 --> 00:22:22,360
(Going crazy)
Going crazy looking for this key clue.

758
00:22:22,440 --> 00:22:24,280
(Next Episode Preview. Golden Key rankings)
How many golden keys does everyone have?

759
00:22:24,640 --> 00:22:26,400
(Warning) Don't ask.
You'll get upset after hearing it.

760
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:28,400
They rank from the lowest.

761
00:22:28,400 --> 00:22:30,120
Ning might break the record.

762
00:22:30,120 --> 00:22:30,720
Really?

763
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:33,400
Yeah, no one had
over seven keys in past seasons.

764
00:22:33,400 --> 00:22:34,880
We should add a rap part to this song.

765
00:22:35,320 --> 00:22:36,200
(Starting with a bang)
♪I want golden keys♪

766
00:22:36,200 --> 00:22:36,920
♪I want golden keys♪

767
00:22:36,920 --> 00:22:38,240
♪How many golden keys do I have now?♪

768
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:39,520
Teach me a few dance moves.

769
00:22:40,100 --> 00:22:41,420
(Easy to handle)

770
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:43,480
So cool.

771
00:22:43,480 --> 00:22:45,440
